  "facts": "Emu War, Campion district, Western Australia, Nov-Dec 1932: about 20,000 emus; Major G.P.W. Meredith with two soldiers, two Lewis guns, 10,000 rounds; emus scattered into small groups; a gun jammed at the dam ambush; troops withdrawn 8 Nov, second attempt until 10 Dec; Meredith reported 986 birds for 9,860 rounds; minimal impact on the emu population; Meredith compared the birds' toughness to tanks (Wikipedia 'Emu War', Britannica).",
